    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a> was created after the crusaders captured and plundered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in April 1204, with a Catholic emperor enthroned in place of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Roman emperors.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> received three eighths of the empire in the Partitio terrarum imperii Romaniae, and its podestà in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> was practically independent of the emperor.</li><li>Constant war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and the Byzantine successor states wore the empire down until a Nicaean force of 800 soldiers took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in July 1261.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>To raise money, Baldwin II stripped the lead roofs of the Great Palace and sold them, handed his only son Philip to Venetian merchants as a guarantee for a loan, and sold the relic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-thorns">Crown of Thorns</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

